les and Columns\n\n#### 1. **machines** table\n- `id` (INTEGER, PRIMARY KEY, AUTOINCREMENT)\n- `machine_id` (TEXT, NOT NULL, UNIQUE) - Format: whoami@hostname\n- `os` (TEXT, NOT NULL) - Operating system (windows/linux/macos)\n- `hostname` (TEXT, NOT NULL) - Hostname parsed from machine_id\n- `username` (TEXT, NOT NULL) - Username parsed from machine_id\n- `first_seen_at` (DATETIME, NOT NULL, DEFAULT: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)\n- `last_seen_at` (DATETIME)\n\n#### 2. **projects** table\n- `id` (INTEGER, PRIMARY KEY, AUTOINCREMENT)\n- `project_slug` (TEXT, NOT NULL, UNIQUE) - Derived from cwd path\n- `project_cwd` (TEXT, NOT NULL) - Working directory path\n- `first_seen_at` (DATETIME, NOT NULL, DEFAULT: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)\n- `last_seen_at` (DATETIME)\n\n#### 3. **sessions** table\n- `id` (INTEGER, PRIMARY KEY, AUTOINCREMENT)\n- `session_id` (TEXT, NOT NULL, UNIQUE)\n- `machine_id` (TEXT, NOT NULL)\n- `os` (TEXT, NOT NULL)\n- `project_slug` (TEXT, NOT NULL)\n- `project_cwd` (TEXT, NOT NULL)\n- `transcript_path` (TEXT, NOT NULL)\n- `local_trace_path` (TEXT)\n- `model` (TEXT)\n- `source` (TEXT)\n- `status` (TEXT, NOT NULL, DEFAULT: 'active')\n- `registered_at` (DATETIME, NOT NULL, DEFAULT: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)\n- `closed_at` (DATETIME)\n- `close_reason` (TEXT)\n\n#### 4. **issue_claims** table\n- `id` (INTEGER, PRIMARY KEY, AUTOINCREMENT)\n- `repo_full_name` (TEXT, NOT NULL) - GitHub repository full name\n- `issue_number` (INTEGER, NOT NULL)\n- `issue_title` (TEXT)\n- `status` (TEXT, NOT NULL, DEFAULT: 'idle')\n- `session_id` (TEXT)\n- `claimed_at` (DATETIME)\n- `updated_at` (DATETIME, NOT NULL, DEFAULT: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)\n- Unique constraint: (repo_full_name, issue_number)\n\n#### 5. **config** table\n- `key` (TEXT, PRIMARY KEY)\n- `value` (TEXT, NOT NULL)\n- `updated_at` (DATETIME, NOT NULL, DEFAULT: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)\n\n#### 6. **proxies** table\n- `proxy_id` (TEXT, PRIMARY KEY)\n- `project_slug` (TEXT, NOT NULL)\n- `status` (TEXT, NOT NULL, DEFAULT: 'active')\n- `registered_at` (DATETIME, NOT NULL)\n- `last_ping_at` (DATETIME)\n\n### API Routes and Methods\n\n#### Health Check\n- `GET /health` - Health check endpoint\n\n#### Issue Routes\n- `GET /api/issue/check` - Check issue status\n- `POST /api/issue/claim` - Claim issue\n- `POST /api/issue/release` - Release issue\n- `POST /api/issue/release-session` - Release all issues for a session\n- `POST /api/issue/status` - Update issue status\n- `GET /api/issues` - List all issues\n\n#### Session Routes\n- `POST /api/session/register` - Register session\n- `POST /api/session/close` - Close session\n- `GET /api/sessions` - List sessions\n- `GET /api/session/{id}/issues` - Get issues for a session\n- `GET /api/session/{id}/tokens` - Get token statistics for a session\n- `GET /api/session/{id}/traces` - Get traces for a session\n- `GET /api/session/{id}` - Get session details\n\n#### Proxy Routes (conditional)\n- `POST /api/proxy/register` - Register proxy\n- `POST /api/proxy/unregister` - Unregister proxy\n- `POST /api/proxy/trace-init` - Forward trace-init\n- `GET /api/proxies` - List proxies\n\n#### Machine Routes (conditional)\n- `GET /api/machines` - List all machines\n\n#### Project Routes (conditional)\n- `GET /api/projects` - List all projects\n\n#### Log Routes (conditional)\n- `GET /api/logs` - Query logs\n\n#### Config Routes (conditional)\n- `GET/PUT /api/config` - Get/update configuration\n\n#### Status Routes (conditional)\n- `GET /api/status` - System status\n\n### Domain Entity Structs and Fields\n\n#### Session struct\n```go\ntype Session struct {\n    ID             int64         // Primary key\n    SessionID      string        // UUID, unique identifier\n    MachineID      string        // whoami@hostname\n    OS             string        // Operating system\n    ProjectSlug    string        // Project identifier\n    ProjectCwd     string        // Working directory path\n    TranscriptPath string        // Path to transcript file\n    LocalTracePath string        // Local trace file path\n    Model          string        // Model used\n    Source         string        // Source (startup/resume)\n    Status         SessionStatus // active/closed\n    RegisteredAt   time.Time     // Registration timestamp\n    ClosedAt       *time.Time    // Closure timestamp (nullable)\n    CloseReason    string        // Reason for closure\n}\n```\n\n#### IssueClaim struct\n```go\ntype IssueClaim struct {\n    ID           int64       // Primary key\n    RepoFullName string      // GitHub repository name\n    IssueNumber  int         // GitHub issue number\n    IssueTitle   string      // Issue title (cached)\n    Status       IssueStatus // Status (idle/claimed/fixing/ready-for-pr/pr-created/testing/reviewing/merged/rejected)\n    SessionID    string      // Session that claimed this issue\n    ClaimedAt    *time.Time  // Claim timestamp (nullable)\n    UpdatedAt    time.Time   // Last update timestamp\n}\n```\n\n#### Machine struct\n```go\ntype Machine struct {\n    ID          int64     // Primary key\n    MachineID   string    // whoami@hostname (unique)\n    OS          string    // Operating system\n    Hostname    string    // Hostname\n    Username    string    // Username\n    FirstSeenAt time.Time // First seen timestamp\n    LastSeenAt  time.Time // Last seen timestamp\n}\n```\n\n#### Project struct\n```go\ntype Project struct {\n    ID          int64     // Primary key\n    ProjectSlug string    // Project identifier (unique)\n    ProjectCwd  string    // Working directory path\n    FirstSeenAt time.Time // First seen timestamp\n    LastSeenAt  time.Time // Last seen timestamp\n}\n```\n\n#### TokenStats struct\n```go\ntype TokenStats struct {\n    APICalls     int // API call count\n    InputTokens  int // Input token count\n    OutputTokens int // Output token count\n    CacheRead    int // Cache read token count\n    CacheCreate  int // Cache create token count\n}\n// Total() method to calculate total tokens\n```\n\n### Key Enumerations\n\n#### SessionStatus\n- `SessionActive` - Active session\n- `SessionClosed` - Closed session\n\n#### IssueStatus\n- `IssueIdle` - Unclaimed\n- `IssueClaimed` - Claimed by a session\n- `IssueFixing` - Under development\n- `IssueReadyForPR` - Ready for PR creation\n- `IssuePRCreated` - PR created\n- `IssueTesting` - In testing phase\n- `IssueReviewing` - Under review\n- `IssueMerged` - Merged (final state)\n- `IssueRejected` - Rejected/returned\n\nThe backend follows a clean architecture with clear separation between domain entities, API handlers, and data storage layer. All database tables have proper indexing for performance, and API routes are RESTful with appropriate HTTP methods."}]}]}
